[a] DrawElements vs DrawArrays
Elements is index based submission whereas Arrays sends the actual Vertex data
For all pratical purposes, stick with the Index based submission


[b] MultiDrawElements and GLSL
    Use ARB_shader_draw_parameters
    gl_DrawIDARB -> in MultiDraw***, this is the drawID and is available in VS

    You can then use this to index into UBOs or other Buffer objects

    To pass this down to FS, use an out variable with the "flat" type attribute.

    This causes it to get passed down to the FS absent any interpolation. Only one of the vertices from the primitive (known as the "provoking vertex")
    will actually get passed down. For other vertices, no data gets passed down.
    https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Primitive#Provoking_vertex

